\frametitle{RDD - Issues}
Your estimate of the treatment effect depends on all these:
			\begin{itemize}
				\item Functional form/line type
				\item Bandwidth (wide vs. narrow)
				\item 	Kernel weighting
			\end{itemize}
			
			Luckily there is an R package that chooses optimal bandwidth and kernel based on fancy algorithms: \texttt{rdrobust}.
			
			For robustness, check what happens if you double/halve the bandwidth, use different kernels and different functional forms
